{"slug":"longest-common-subsequence","title":"Longest Common Subsequence","level":"Medium","summary":"Return the length of the longest subsequence common to both strings (0 if none).","method":"longestCommonSubsequence","params":[["String","text1"],["String","text2"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["\"abcde\"","\"ace\""],"out":"3"},{"in":["\"abc\"","\"abc\""],"out":"3"},{"in":["\"abc\"","\"def\""],"out":"0"},{"in":["\"bsbininm\"","\"jmjkbkjkv\""],"out":"1"},{"in":["\"ezupkr\"","\"ubmrapg\""],"out":"2"},{"in":["\"a\"","\"a\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"ttuuiizti\"","\"ttizt\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["\"z\"","\"z\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"b\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"babbbababaa\"","\"abbbaba\""],"out":"7","g":1},{"in":["\"c\"","\"ab\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"bba\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"bab\"","\"bba\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaa\"","\"bbab\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"aca\"","\"cacbabbaaa\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"aabbaaaa\"","\"abbaabbbabb\""],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["\"ababa\"","\"bab\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"qqnqggoogo\"","\"e\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"aa\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"c\"","\"c\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"o\"","\"bdfsyrg\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"egag\"","\"xzmgimgdbuze\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"hfn\"","\"nfpeze\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"ccbb\"","\"abbbaab\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"bababa\"","\"bcbabcbb\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"bba\"","\"b\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"aba\"","\"a\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"cab\"","\"a\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"cg\"","\"rrrrrr\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"bb\"","\"c\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"apse\"","\"k\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"cc\"","\"a\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"abbbbba\"","\"abbba\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["\"bca\"","\"ca\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"znm\"","\"fffffff\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"aba\"","\"ababbabbb\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"aab\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"ababab\"","\"abab\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"abbbaba\"","\"aaa\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"ytgdp\"","\"yp\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"baacbacaba\"","\"ac\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"bb\"","\"bb\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"babbbbabbb\"","\"babbbabb\""],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["\"ccbacbabaacaacacccac\"","\"abbcacacca\""],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["\"abbccbcbbba\"","\"cbac\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#3:3e059c181449fa91\"","perf":{"label":"two 1,000-character strings","gen":"String a0 = BCB.str(1000, \"abcde\"); String a1 = BCB.str(1000, \"abcde\");","floorMs":2000},"refMs":14}],"lesson":"dp-strings","anchor":"longest-common-subsequence","statement":"Return the length of the longest common subsequence of `text1` and `text2`, or `0` if they share none.\n\nA subsequence keeps the original order of characters but may skip some, so `\"ace\"` is a subsequence of `\"abcde\"`.","constraints":["1 <= text1.length, text2.length <= 1000","Both strings have only lowercase English letters"],"hints":["Compare the last characters. If they match, they can end the common subsequence; if not, one of them must be dropped.","L[i][j] = L[i − 1][j − 1] + 1 if text1[i − 1] == text2[j − 1], otherwise max(L[i − 1][j], L[i][j − 1]).","The table is (m + 1) × (n + 1) with zeros in row 0 and column 0. Two rows are enough for O(n) space."],"explain":"\"ace\" appears in both strings with its letters in order (a, c and e are picked from \"abcde\" skipping b and d). No longer common subsequence exists, so the answer is 3."},
{"slug":"delete-operation-for-two-strings","title":"Delete Operation for Two Strings","level":"Medium","summary":"Each step deletes one character from either string. Return the fewest steps to make the two strings equal.","method":"minDistance","params":[["String","word1"],["String","word2"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["\"sea\"","\"eat\""],"out":"2"},{"in":["\"leetcode\"","\"etco\""],"out":"4"},{"in":["\"a\"","\"a\""],"out":"0"},{"in":["\"abc\"","\"xyz\""],"out":"6"},{"in":["\"intention\"","\"execution\""],"out":"8"},{"in":["\"bba\"","\"babbbbbbb\""],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"b\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"cbccbc\"","\"cbccbc\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"c\"","\"c\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"c\"","\"cbba\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"sssaesaseee\"","\"sase\""],"out":"7","g":1},{"in":["\"abbb\"","\"b\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"acb\"","\"abbcacc\""],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["\"e\"","\"e\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"abbbbaabbaabbabb\"","\"babb\""],"out":"12","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbaaabbabbaabbabbaa\"","\"aaabbababbabaa\""],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["\"aaeaa\"","\"s\""],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["\"cbbb\"","\"c\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"bca\"","\"cabbacb\""],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["\"ccc\"","\"c\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"acb\"","\"b\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"aeaaasaeaa\"","\"eaee\""],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["\"ae\"","\"s\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"ba\"","\"ab\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"aa\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbababbba\"","\"bbababba\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"essessssses\"","\"esssses\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"es\"","\"s\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"eese\"","\"eesseseeseae\""],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["\"cacaacbb\"","\"baaaaababb\""],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["\"ba\"","\"aaa\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"abaabbb\"","\"b\""],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["\"aeaas\"","\"seaeeseae\""],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["\"eee\"","\"sssseasa\""],"out":"9","g":1},{"in":["\"sa\"","\"aa\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"b\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaabbbaab\"","\"aaabbba\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"sass\"","\"sas\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"ses\"","\"es\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"saseeaeassasaasseese\"","\"saseassasasseese\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"e\"","\"easaaaeasae\""],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["\"cc\"","\"cc\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"bb\"","\"bbbbbba\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["\"aaeeeeessaa\"","\"ea\""],"out":"9","g":1},{"in":["\"bbabbbb\"","\"cac\""],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#3:6056ae1827a1f5d0\"","perf":{"label":"two 500-character strings","gen":"String a0 = BCB.str(500, \"abc\"); String a1 = BCB.str(500, \"abc\");","floorMs":2000},"refMs":10}],"lesson":"dp-strings","statement":"In one step you may delete exactly one character from either `word1` or `word2`. Return the minimum number of steps needed to make the two strings equal.\n\nThe strings end up equal to a common subsequence of both, so the fewest deletions keep their longest common subsequence: the answer is `len(word1) + len(word2) − 2 × LCS`.","constraints":["1 <= word1.length, word2.length <= 500","Both strings have only lowercase English letters"],"hints":["The characters you keep form a common subsequence. To delete as little as possible, keep the longest one.","Compute the longest common subsequence L.","The answer is (word1.length − L) + (word2.length − L). A direct DP on deletions works too."],"explain":"Delete \"s\" from \"sea\" and \"t\" from \"eat\"; both become \"ea\". That takes 2 steps, the fewest possible."},
{"slug":"longest-palindromic-substring","title":"Longest Palindromic Substring","level":"Medium","summary":"Return a longest substring of s that is a palindrome. Any palindrome of the maximum length is accepted.","method":"longestPalindrome","params":[["String","s"]],"returns":"String","check":"custom:palindrome","tests":[{"in":["\"babad\""],"out":"\"bab\""},{"in":["\"cbbd\""],"out":"\"bb\""},{"in":["\"a\""],"out":"\"a\""},{"in":["\"forgeeksskeegfor\""],"out":"\"geeksskeeg\""},{"in":["\"abcda\""],"out":"\"a\""},{"in":["\"bcacbacbbbccababacacac\""],"out":"\"cababac\"","g":1},{"in":["\"1AAaA11AA\""],"out":"\"A11A\"","g":1},{"in":["\"abbaabaaaaaabbbbab\""],"out":"\"baaaaaab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"v\""],"out":"\"v\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\""],"out":"\"aa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"zwetwzee\""],"out":"\"ee\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbaabbbabababb\""],"out":"\"bbabababb\"","g":1},{"in":["\"11A\""],"out":"\"11\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cbcbcaaccac\""],"out":"\"cbcbc\"","g":1},{"in":["\"mtzhsh\""],"out":"\"hsh\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cccabcb\""],"out":"\"ccc\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaabbaaaaabbbabbbaaaaabbaaba\""],"out":"\"aabbaaaaabbbabbbaaaaabbaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aabbaabaabbaabb\""],"out":"\"aabbaabaabbaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbaba\""],"out":"\"bab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cbcbcb\""],"out":"\"cbcbc\"","g":1},{"in":["\"a11Aa1a1111a1aa1\""],"out":"\"a1a1111a1a\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbaabbaaaaabbab\""],"out":"\"abbaaaaabba\"","g":1},{"in":["\"z\""],"out":"\"z\"","g":1},{"in":["\"abbbaabbaabbbaabba\""],"out":"\"abbbaabbaabbba\"","g":1},{"in":["\"11a1a1aAaAa\""],"out":"\"1a1a1\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aabcbcacbbcabcbbbbccacccbcccbc\""],"out":"\"cccbccc\"","g":1},{"in":["\"A11AaA1Aa\""],"out":"\"1AaA1\"","g":1},{"in":["\"gbppxfwwfxppna\""],"out":"\"ppxfwwfxpp\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbabaabab\""],"out":"\"babaabab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bccabb\""],"out":"\"cc\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cacacbaaaccbccaaabcacabb\""],"out":"\"acacbaaaccbccaaabcaca\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"1\""],"out":"\"1\"","g":1},{"in":["\"AA1Aa11\""],"out":"\"A1A\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aab\""],"out":"\"aa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbaaaabaabababaabaabb\""],"out":"\"aabaabababaabaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaababaab\""],"out":"\"aababaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aabcbbabcacacccbbcaacbac\""],"out":"\"bcaacb\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbaabbbaab\""],"out":"\"baabbbaab\"","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#2:8030507b4c32092\"","perf":{"label":"a 1,000-character string (length compared)","gen":"String a0 = BCB.str(1000, \"ab\");","call":"Object r = s.longestPalindrome(a0).length();","floorMs":2000},"refMs":1}],"lesson":"dp-strings","anchor":"longest-palindromic-substring--expand-around-centres","statement":"Return a longest contiguous substring of `s` that reads the same forwards and backwards.\n\nIf several substrings share the maximum length, any of them is accepted.\n\nA substring is contiguous: its characters sit next to each other in `s`. Every single character is a palindrome, so the answer is never empty.","constraints":["1 <= s.length <= 1000","`s` has only digits and English letters"],"hints":["Every palindrome mirrors around its centre, and a centre is either one character or the gap between two.","For each of the 2n − 1 centres, expand outward while the characters on both sides match.","Keep the longest expansion. That is O(n²) time and O(1) space. A DP table isPal[i][j] also works, and Manacher's algorithm is O(n)."],"explain":"\"bab\" reads the same both ways and no palindrome in \"babad\" is longer than 3. \"aba\" is just as long and would also be accepted; the example shows \"bab\"."},
{"slug":"longest-palindromic-subsequence","title":"Longest Palindromic Subsequence","level":"Medium","summary":"Return the length of the longest subsequence of s that is a palindrome.","method":"longestPalindromeSubseq","params":[["String","s"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["\"bbbab\""],"out":"4"},{"in":["\"cbbd\""],"out":"2"},{"in":["\"a\""],"out":"1"},{"in":["\"agbdba\""],"out":"5"},{"in":["\"abcdef\""],"out":"1"},{"in":["\"llllllllll\""],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["\"bb\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaa\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaa\""],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["\"s\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"ggggg\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"aba\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"b\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbacbcaa\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["\"aaa\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"p\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbbbbbbbb\""],"out":"11","g":1},{"in":["\"bacaababbbbcbbcabaaaababcac\""],"out":"18","g":1},{"in":["\"baababaabbabaaabababaaaabbabba\""],"out":"25","g":1},{"in":["\"hvhvhvrvrvvvvrrvhhvrrvvvhvhrhv\""],"out":"22","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"11","g":1},{"in":["\"ba\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbbbbbb\""],"out":"9","g":1},{"in":["\"reybi\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"wvh\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"c\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"bbca\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"ab\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaa\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaa\""],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["\"aabbbbb\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["\"ababbbaa\""],"out":"7","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbb\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"abacac\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"g\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\""],"out":"22","g":1},{"in":["\"r\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"qss\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"rrzaa\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"abbbbbbaabbabbab\""],"out":"12","g":1},{"in":["\"bbabbaabb\""],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["\"uuulluluuu\""],"out":"9","g":1},{"in":["\"wjk\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"cbabbca\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#3:34ef6a180f05a611\"","perf":{"label":"a 1,000-character string","gen":"String a0 = BCB.str(1000, \"abc\");","floorMs":2000},"refMs":13}],"lesson":"dp-strings","anchor":"longest-palindromic-subsequence","statement":"Return the length of the longest subsequence of `s` that is a palindrome. A subsequence keeps the order of characters but may skip some.\n\nFor example in \"cbbd\" the longest palindromic subsequence is \"bb\", of length 2.","constraints":["1 <= s.length <= 1000","`s` has only lowercase English letters"],"hints":["Look at the two ends of the range s[i..j]. If they are equal, both can be in the palindrome.","P[i][j] = P[i + 1][j − 1] + 2 if s[i] == s[j], otherwise max(P[i + 1][j], P[i][j − 1]); P[i][i] = 1.","Fill by increasing length (or i from the end). It is also the LCS of s and reverse(s)."],"explain":"Skipping the \"a\" leaves \"bbbb\", a palindrome of length 4. Keeping all five characters gives \"bbbab\", which is not a palindrome, so the answer is 4."},
{"slug":"palindromic-substrings","title":"Palindromic Substrings","level":"Medium","summary":"Count the substrings of s that are palindromes (substrings at different positions count separately).","method":"countSubstrings","params":[["String","s"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["\"abc\""],"out":"3"},{"in":["\"aaa\""],"out":"6"},{"in":["\"a\""],"out":"1"},{"in":["\"abba\""],"out":"6"},{"in":["\"racecar\""],"out":"10"},{"in":["\"eodpzirttyqcxxqdtorxmykq\""],"out":"26","g":1},{"in":["\"buf\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"ba\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"b\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"x\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"yyyyyyyyyyy\""],"out":"66","g":1},{"in":["\"accifauzectmednjhventxkeusvuwj\""],"out":"31","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"k\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"brjigsoww\""],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["\"aaabababcbabacbcccbbcaaba\""],"out":"49","g":1},{"in":["\"bcc\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaa\""],"out":"21","g":1},{"in":["\"bbcb\""],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["\"mtmhmtmhmhh\""],"out":"21","g":1},{"in":["\"acacbacb\""],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["\"hkqlvlawpiq\""],"out":"12","g":1},{"in":["\"c\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"caab\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbbab\""],"out":"18","g":1},{"in":["\"baca\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["\"zh\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"baabb\""],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"55","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaa\""],"out":"36","g":1},{"in":["\"lvfi\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"pjjxmwkyk\""],"out":"11","g":1},{"in":["\"rhcujlb\""],"out":"7","g":1},{"in":["\"cbc\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"bab\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"78","g":1},{"in":["\"aabbaaaba\""],"out":"18","g":1},{"in":["\"ababbaa\""],"out":"12","g":1},{"in":["\"babba\""],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["\"y\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"ytmfnp\""],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"351","g":1},{"in":["\"abaababaa\""],"out":"19","g":1},{"in":["\"dsw\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaa\""],"out":"15","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#4:630321024247f5a0\"","perf":{"label":"a 1,000-character string","gen":"String a0 = BCB.str(1000, \"ab\");","floorMs":2000},"refMs":1}],"lesson":"dp-strings","statement":"Count the substrings of `s` that are palindromes. Substrings at different positions are counted separately even if they contain the same characters.\n\nFor example \"aaa\" has 6 palindromic substrings: three single \"a\"s, two \"aa\"s and \"aaa\" itself.","constraints":["1 <= s.length <= 1000","`s` has only lowercase English letters"],"hints":["Every palindromic substring has a centre: a single character or the gap between two characters.","Expand around each of the 2n − 1 centres and count every step at which the two sides still match.","That counts each palindrome exactly once, in O(n²) time and O(1) space."],"explain":"The palindromic substrings of \"abc\" are \"a\", \"b\" and \"c\". No longer substring reads the same backwards, so the answer is 3."},
{"slug":"interleaving-string","title":"Interleaving String","level":"Medium","summary":"Return whether s3 can be formed by interleaving s1 and s2, keeping each string's characters in their original order.","method":"isInterleave","params":[["String","s1"],["String","s2"],["String","s3"]],"returns":"boolean","tests":[{"in":["\"aabcc\"","\"dbbca\"","\"aadbbcbcac\""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\"aabcc\"","\"dbbca\"","\"aadbbbaccc\""],"out":"false"},{"in":["\"\"","\"\"","\"\""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\"a\"","\"\"","\"a\""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\"ab\"","\"cd\"","\"acdb\""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\"aaaaa\"","\"aaaaaaaaa\"","\"aaazaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"babbb\"","\"ba\"","\"babbbb\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"aaa\"","\"\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"ccccaabacc\"","\"ccccac\"","\"ccccccccaabacacc\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aab\"","\"\"","\"aab\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"baabbba\"","\"ab\"","\"ba\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"a\"","\"a\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbabb\"","\"\"","\"bbbazb\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"abb\"","\"b\"","\"abbb\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"\"","\"aa\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"abbaaaa\"","\"\"","\"abbaaab\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"aaaaaaaaa\"","\"aaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"ab\"","\"aa\"","\"b\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"ccbbaaabc\"","\"aa\"","\"cacbzbaaabc\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"c\"","\"cc\"","\"acccbaabaaabccaacbb\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"ccbc\"","\"ba\"","\"baccb\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"abbba\"","\"\"","\"abbb\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaabbb\"","\"bb\"","\"aabbaaaabb\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"\"","\"aaaaaaaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"aa\"","\"aaaa\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"cbabacacac\"","\"\"","\"cbabacacac\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"cabab\"","\"caba\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aaacc\"","\"bacabcacc\"","\"baaaacccabcaca\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaa\"","\"aa\"","\"aaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bbb\"","\"aabbbabbba\"","\"bababbbbabbba\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"abc\"","\"ccbbacc\"","\"\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"aaaaaaaa\"","\"aaaaaaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaa\"","\"aaaaaa\"","\"aaaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"\"","\"a\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aabbbabbb\"","\"b\"","\"aabbbbabbb\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"accbbabca\"","\"\"","\"\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"cac\"","\"bbbc\"","\"bcacbbc\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"ab\"","\"abb\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"ccbcccab\"","\"bcacbca\"","\"cc\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"aaaaaaaa\"","\"aaaaaaaa\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aaabb\"","\"cb\"","\"ccbaabb\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"bb\"","\"bb\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"bababa\"","\"b\"","\"bbabab\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"ccbbb\"","\"\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aabaabbb\"","\"bbbbbbabab\"","\"baabababbbbbbbabab\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#5:b5fae2c14238b978\"","perf":{"label":"100 + 100 characters","gen":"String a0 = \"a\".repeat(100); String a1 = \"a\".repeat(99) + \"b\"; String a2 = \"a\".repeat(200);","floorMs":2000},"refMs":1}],"lesson":"dp-strings","anchor":"interleaving-string","statement":"Return `true` if `s3` can be formed by interleaving `s1` and `s2`: merging their characters into one string while keeping the characters of each in their original order.\n\nFor example, `\"aadbbcbcac\"` interleaves `\"aabcc\"` and `\"dbbca\"`.","constraints":["0 <= s1.length, s2.length <= 100","0 <= s3.length <= 200","All strings have only lowercase English letters"],"hints":["If the lengths do not add up, the answer is false. Greedy matching fails when both strings could supply the next character.","ok[i][j] means \"the first i characters of s1 and the first j of s2 can form the first i + j of s3\".","ok[i][j] = (ok[i − 1][j] && s1[i − 1] == s3[i + j − 1]) || (ok[i][j − 1] && s2[j − 1] == s3[i + j − 1]), with ok[0][0] = true."],"explain":"Split s1 as \"aa\" + \"bc\" + \"c\" and s2 as \"dbbc\" + \"a\". Alternating the pieces gives \"aa\" + \"dbbc\" + \"bc\" + \"a\" + \"c\" = \"aadbbcbcac\", which is s3, so the answer is `true`."},
{"slug":"edit-distance","title":"Edit Distance","level":"Medium","summary":"Return the fewest insertions, deletions and replacements of single characters that turn word1 into word2.","method":"minDistance","params":[["String","word1"],["String","word2"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["\"horse\"","\"ros\""],"out":"3"},{"in":["\"intention\"","\"execution\""],"out":"5"},{"in":["\"\"","\"abc\""],"out":"3"},{"in":["\"same\"","\"same\""],"out":"0"},{"in":["\"kitten\"","\"sitting\""],"out":"3"},{"in":["\"heeereerhr\"","\"hrssrhshhshs\""],"out":"9","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"shhshsheoo\""],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"horr\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbb\"","\"bbbaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"bba\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"baaaaaab\""],"out":"7","g":1},{"in":["\"sreoh\"","\"ro\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"abacaba\"","\"aacbaaca\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"sosrs\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"sss\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"bb\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"bbabbbbab\""],"out":"9","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"ro\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"bbc\"","\"ccbbaaca\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"ac\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"cb\"","\"cbac\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"orreosseoseerr\"","\"ho\""],"out":"13","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"cbcbac\""],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["\"oerheee\"","\"eerohrrsoe\""],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["\"eeseessee\"","\"eh\""],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["\"cccbaabac\"","\"cabaaccc\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"aaabbbbbab\"","\"\""],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"aabbccaab\""],"out":"9","g":1},{"in":["\"oreshhshrehoer\"","\"ross\""],"out":"11","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"os\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"ababaaba\"","\"aaabaabab\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"ro\"","\"ehosss\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["\"babbbabaaabb\"","\"aaaab\""],"out":"7","g":1},{"in":["\"c\"","\"cc\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"eeheoehesrsh\""],"out":"12","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"bbbaccb\""],"out":"7","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"bababbabbbabb\""],"out":"13","g":1},{"in":["\"ccaaabb\"","\"abbaacbbc\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"cacbbbbbaaccb\""],"out":"12","g":1},{"in":["\"eoo\"","\"shosse\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["\"roe\"","\"oeo\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"abaaab\""],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"bbbbbb\""],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["\"aac\"","\"aacac\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"abbaabbaba\""],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#3:6037bb1827875b58\"","perf":{"label":"two 500-character strings","gen":"String a0 = BCB.str(500, \"abcd\"); String a1 = BCB.str(500, \"abcd\");","floorMs":2000},"refMs":16}],"lesson":"dp-strings","anchor":"edit-distance--three-operations-three-neighbours","statement":"Return the minimum number of operations that turn `word1` into `word2`. Each operation inserts, deletes or replaces a single character.\n\nFor example turning \"intention\" into \"execution\" takes 5 operations. Each operation changes exactly one character.","constraints":["0 <= word1.length, word2.length <= 500","Both strings have only lowercase English letters"],"hints":["Look at the last characters of the prefixes word1[0..i) and word2[0..j). If they match, no operation is needed for them.","Otherwise D[i][j] = 1 + min(D[i − 1][j] (delete), D[i][j − 1] (insert), D[i − 1][j − 1] (replace)).","D[i][0] = i and D[0][j] = j. Two rows are enough."],"explain":"Replace \"h\" with \"r\" (\"horse\" → \"rorse\"), delete the second \"r\" (\"rose\"), then delete \"e\" (\"ros\"). Three operations, and no shorter sequence works, so the answer is 3."},
{"slug":"distinct-subsequences","title":"Distinct Subsequences","level":"Hard","summary":"Return how many distinct subsequences of s equal t (the answer fits in 32 bits).","method":"numDistinct","params":[["String","s"],["String","t"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["\"rabbbit\"","\"rabbit\""],"out":"3"},{"in":["\"babgbag\"","\"bag\""],"out":"5"},{"in":["\"a\"","\"b\""],"out":"0"},{"in":["\"aaaa\"","\"aa\""],"out":"6"},{"in":["\"aAAAAAaAaaaaaaaAaaAa\"","\"aAAAAaaaaaaAa\""],"out":"2520","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"a\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"aaab\"","\"ab\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"ab\"","\"a\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbacbcc\"","\"bbbcb\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"aa\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"babba\"","\"ba\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"AAaaa\"","\"aAa\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"abacaabbbc\"","\"aacabb\""],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["\"bb\"","\"bb\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaAaaAaaa\"","\"aAaa\""],"out":"45","g":1},{"in":["\"AaAaaaAaA\"","\"aAaAaAaA\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"cbbabaab\"","\"baa\""],"out":"7","g":1},{"in":["\"A\"","\"AaAAaa\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"AaAaAaAAAAAAaAAaAaaAA\"","\"a\""],"out":"7","g":1},{"in":["\"t\"","\"a\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"bccbbcaa\"","\"abbbbbac\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"t\"","\"abr\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"A\"","\"A\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"ccbc\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"bbaaaab\"","\"a\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"brbirbtrtrrrbibtbttitrtbi\"","\"iiaa\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"i\"","\"taiabair\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"atrabrbrababrt\"","\"iiiiair\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"aaA\"","\"aA\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"aAAAaAaaa\"","\"aaAaAAA\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"Aa\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"c\"","\"babaca\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"b\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"aAAaAAAaaAaAaaAAAaAaaAaa\"","\"Aaa\""],"out":"331","g":1},{"in":["\"ababaabb\"","\"a\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbacbbb\"","\"bbcbb\""],"out":"9","g":1},{"in":["\"AaA\"","\"A\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"aA\"","\"A\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"ttbt\"","\"ratar\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"cabaccbca\"","\"ccc\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"abiai\"","\"biai\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"ab\"","\"bbba\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"baaaa\"","\"tttttt\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"iiibbi\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#7:c1343dff145b11e4\"","perf":{"label":"a 1,000-character string","gen":"String a0 = BCB.str(1000, \"abc\"); String a1 = \"abc\";","floorMs":2000},"refMs":1}],"lesson":"dp-strings","anchor":"distinct-subsequences","statement":"Return the number of distinct subsequences of `s` that equal `t`. Two subsequences are different if they use different positions of `s`.\n\nThe answer fits in a 32-bit signed integer.\n\nThe characters of `t` must be matched in order, but they don't have to be next to each other in `s`.","constraints":["1 <= s.length, t.length <= 1000","Both strings have only English letters"],"hints":["Count the ways to match t[0..j) using s[0..i). The new character s[i − 1] can be used for t[j − 1] if they are equal, or skipped.","W[i][j] = W[i − 1][j] + (s[i − 1] == t[j − 1] ? W[i − 1][j − 1] : 0), with W[i][0] = 1.","With a one-dimensional array, update j from right to left. Intermediate values can exceed an int, so use a long or guard them."],"explain":"\"rabbbit\" has three b's and \"rabbit\" needs two of them. Skipping the first, second or third b gives 3 different choices of positions, so the answer is 3."},
{"slug":"regular-expression-matching","title":"Regular Expression Matching","level":"Hard","summary":"Match the whole string s against pattern p, where \".\" matches any character and \"*\" matches zero or more of the preceding element.","method":"isMatch","params":[["String","s"],["String","p"]],"returns":"boolean","tests":[{"in":["\"aa\"","\"a\""],"out":"false"},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"a*\""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\"ab\"","\".*\""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\"aab\"","\"c*a*b\""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\"mississippi\"","\"mis*is*p*.\""],"out":"false"},{"in":["\"\"","\"a*b*\""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\"aacabbb\"","\"aa.ab*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaa\"","\"a*a.\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"cb\"","\"cb*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\".*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"aa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaa\"","\"a.a*aa..*a*.\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"bb*b*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aaa\"","\"aaa\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaa\"","\".aaaa*aa\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"aa*.a*aa*a*\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\".*a\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\".a.\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"abb\"","\"ab*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"bbaaaab\"","\"aa*aab*\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"abbbbcc\"","\"ab*bc*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"bba\"","\"bba\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"bb\"","\"c*.*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaa\"","\"a*a*.a*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\".a*.\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"aa*.*.a*\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaa\"","\"aaa*aa.*a\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"bbaaaaab\"","\".baa*a*.b*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"babbbbabba\"","\"bbab\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"baaa\"","\"bc*a*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aabbbabaaa\"","\"a*b*a.*aa.*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaa\"","\"aaaa*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"abccac\"","\"c*abca*ca*b\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"ccccca\"","\"c*ccca\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"ccbca\"","\"a*.c*bc*a\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\"bbb.*a\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aaa\"","\"a*.a*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\".\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"\"","\".a*b*\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbb\"","\"b.*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"baaba\"","\"ba*ba\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaa\"","\"aaaa*a*a\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"abaaa\"","\".ba*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaa\"","\"a.a.a.*a*\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aac\"","\"aac\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"cbaaaa\"","\"c.*ba*a\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#5:b5fae2c14238b978\"","perf":{"label":"a pattern that defeats plain backtracking","gen":"String a0 = \"a\".repeat(20) + \"b\"; String a1 = \"a*\".repeat(10) + \"c\";","floorMs":2000},"refMs":1}],"lesson":"dp-strings","statement":"Implement matching of a pattern `p` against the whole string `s` (not just a part of it), where:\n\n- `.` matches any single character,\n- `*` matches zero or more copies of the element just before it.\n\nEvery `*` in the pattern has a valid character or `.` before it.","constraints":["0 <= s.length <= 21","1 <= p.length <= 21","`s` has only lowercase letters; `p` has lowercase letters, \".\" and \"*\""],"hints":["Plain recursion branches at every \"*\" and can take exponential time on patterns like \"a*a*a*…c\". Memoise it.","M[i][j] means s[i..] matches p[j..]. If p[j + 1] is \"*\", either skip \"x*\" (M[i][j + 2]) or, if s[i] matches x, consume one character (M[i + 1][j]).","Otherwise the characters must match and you move on: first-match && M[i + 1][j + 1]. The base case is the end of the pattern."],"explain":"The pattern \"a\" matches exactly one \"a\", but `s` is \"aa\" and the whole string must match. So the answer is `false`."}
